Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.15,0:00:09.01,Default,,0,0,0,,YAMU! YAMU! YAMU! YAMU! YAMU!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.41,0:00:31.53,Default,,0,0,0,,You're on the move!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.51,0:01:10.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Embarrassing you in front of millions\Nof people is more fun than I imagined.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.17,0:01:13.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, let the humiliation continue.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.01,0:01:16.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I activate the power of Nibelung's ring.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.89,0:01:20.77,Default,,0,0,0,,This forces you to draw two cards,\Nand if there are any monsters,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.03,0:01:22.59,Default,,0,0,0,,they're immediately destroyed.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.67,0:01:24.38,Default,,0,0,0,,And you think that scares me?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.55,0:01:25.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, think again.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.05,0:01:27.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Now let's get this over with.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.87,0:01:30.25,Default,,0,0,0,,It looks like you're out of luck.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.43,0:01:31.85,Default,,0,0,0,,No monsters here.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.11,0:01:34.47,Default,,0,0,0,,So, I'll place this face down.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.69,0:01:38.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, since there's nothing else you\Ncan do, I assume that ends your turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.03,0:01:42.83,Default,,0,0,0,,After all, my ring has rendered\Nyour dragon cannon useless.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.91,0:01:44.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Uh-oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.95,0:01:46.47,Default,,0,0,0,,This doesn't look good, guys.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.55,0:01:48.49,Default,,0,0,0,,You know what's next, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.11,0:01:53.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Valkyra Zwei, use your fortune chariot\Nand attack his life points directly.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.25,0:01:59.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I activate my trap card!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.93,0:02:01.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Attack Guidance Armor!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.37,0:02:05.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Now your attack gets redirected\Nto your other monster!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.73,0:02:12.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I have a little trap card of\Nmy own, so my Valkyrie is safe!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.45,0:02:16.67,Default,,0,0,0,,How, you ask?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.83,0:02:18.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, that's the beauty\Nof Wotan's judgment!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.07,0:02:24.19,Default,,0,0,0,,By switching one magic card from my\Nhand with the top card off my deck,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.43,0:02:27.67,Default,,0,0,0,,I am able to instantly end\Nthe battle phase of my turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.05,0:02:31.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, let's see if fate\Nwas good to me, shall we?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.23,0:02:35.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Lovely, just lovely.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.29,0:02:38.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks to you, I've assembled\Nthree of my most powerful cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.77,0:02:42.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, help me welcome...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.51,0:02:52.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Those dames are nothing but bad news.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.67,0:02:54.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, he played them last time.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.81,0:02:57.49,Default,,0,0,0,,They nearly destroyed your deck. Look,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.81,0:03:01.09,Default,,0,0,0,,that lame strategy may have worked\Nagainst a dork like Wheeler,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.17,0:03:02.94,Default,,0,0,0,,but I'm in a different league.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.09,0:03:04.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, is that so?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.59,0:03:07.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Why don't we let my goddesses\Nbe the judge of that
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.13,0:03:10.15,Default,,0,0,0,,By having a look at the top\Nthree cards of your deck.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.23,0:03:12.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, Goddess Skulld,\NProtector of the Future,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.21,0:03:15.95,Default,,0,0,0,,show me what destiny holds for her Kaiba.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.53,0:03:21.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Impossible!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.57,0:03:23.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Three Blue-Eyes White Dragons?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.63,0:03:29.98,Default,,0,0,0,,By the expression on your face, I'm\Nguessing my destiny looks pretty good.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.19,0:03:33.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, you verdume the\Nmoment you decided to duel me.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.87,0:03:37.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I call upon my goddess\NMordanda, protector of the present.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.63,0:03:40.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Time for me to guess your top card.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.19,0:03:42.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll say it's a monster.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.77,0:03:46.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Gee, how'd you ever guess?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.03,0:03:49.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Just place it on the\Nfield in defense mode.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.73,0:03:50.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Sure, whatever.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.43,0:03:58.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I'll remove that very card from the\Ngame by correctly predicting its identity.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.99,0:04:02.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Goddess Earl, protector\Nof the past, guide me.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.97,0:04:06.85,Default,,0,0,0,,I predict the card you just played\Nis your blue-eyes white dragon!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.79,0:04:16.71,Default,,0,0,0,,It's gone!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.03,0:04:17.97,Default,,0,0,0,,This is bad!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.51,0:04:20.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Why the long face? Oh, right.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.15,0:04:23.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I destroyed your favorite monster.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.55,0:04:26.35,Default,,0,0,0,,But that's just the beginning, Herr Kaiba.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.97,0:04:31.31,Default,,0,0,0,,You and your company have been a\Nthorn in my side since the day we met,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.39,0:04:34.43,Default,,0,0,0,,So it's time to remove\Nyou once and for all.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.77,0:04:38.39,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll take it from here.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.69,0:04:40.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold on.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.79,0:04:42.19,Default,,0,0,0,,How soon we forget.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.59,0:04:44.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Your dragon is wearing my ring.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.79,0:04:48.25,Default,,0,0,0,,So the card you just drew goes\Nstraight to the graveyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.79,0:04:54.15,Default,,0,0,0,,And since you can't attack, I can\Nonly assume you're ending your turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.59,0:04:55.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Will you assume wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.29,0:04:59.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I play Monster Reborn. You what?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.49,0:05:01.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, show yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.39,0:05:03.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Blue-Eyes White Dragon!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.03,0:05:09.77,Default,,0,0,0,,That's what I'm talking about!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.85,0:05:11.29,Default,,0,0,0,,In your face, Siegfried!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.37,0:05:14.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Nobody comes between me and my Blue-Eyes!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.49,0:05:17.47,Default,,0,0,0,,And anyone foolish enough\Nto try pays the price!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.69,0:05:24.81,Default,,0,0,0,,What happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.11,0:05:26.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I gave up my chariot!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.77,0:05:29.49,Default,,0,0,0,,So my Valkyrie's vile remains unharmed!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.47,0:05:32.39,Default,,0,0,0,,But your life points don't.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.59,0:05:34.69,Default,,0,0,0,,It looks like the same old story.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.03,0:05:38.39,Default,,0,0,0,,I rise to the top and you\Nget lost in my shadow.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.39,0:05:40.27,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll see.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.53,0:05:43.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, I invoke the power of my goddesses.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.29,0:05:46.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Show me his top three cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.75,0:05:52.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Place the third card on\Nthe top of your deck.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.37,0:05:57.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Now all I have to do is call its\Nname and it's removed from plague.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.15,0:06:00.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Luster Dragon number two!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.01,0:06:10.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Next, I activate a magic card\Nknown as Griffon's Feather Duster.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.95,0:06:16.57,Default,,0,0,0,,First, it takes away every magic and\Ntrap card on my side of the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.03,0:06:21.17,Default,,0,0,0,,But then it leaves me with 500\Nextra life points for each one.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.37,0:06:26.37,Default,,0,0,0,,He just got back everything\NBlue Eyes took away!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.45,0:06:32.15,Default,,0,0,0,,And then finally, I'll sacrifice my\NValkyrie Öster and my Valkyrie Zweig.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.41,0:06:39.47,Default,,0,0,0,,That lets me summon my Valkyrie\NBrunhilde in defense mode.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.11,0:06:50.47,Default,,0,0,0,,And by the way, sorry\Nto ruin the surprise,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.75,0:06:55.45,Default,,0,0,0,,but the card you're about to draw is a\Nmonster and unfortunately it won't last long.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.53,0:06:57.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Do I care? No.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.87,0:06:59.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, you should.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.59,0:07:01.85,Default,,0,0,0,,I activate Nibelung's ring.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.39,0:07:04.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Your monster is no more!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.97,0:07:08.27,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't need that card anyway.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.97,0:07:12.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Not when I have blue eyes. Attack now!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.33,0:07:23.57,Default,,0,0,0,,No way!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.65,0:07:29.57,Default,,0,0,0,,As you can see, Brunhilde escaped without\Na scratch, thanks to her special ability.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.87,0:07:32.75,Default,,0,0,0,,But all I had to do was\Nlower her defense points.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.61,0:07:35.27,Default,,0,0,0,,I place this face down.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.35,0:07:36.97,Default,,0,0,0,,That ends my turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.35,0:07:39.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Another move wasted.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.43,0:07:42.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Eventually, your girlfriend's gonna\Nrun out of points, and when she does,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.05,0:07:44.46,Default,,0,0,0,,my dragon'll be waiting.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.73,0:07:46.67,Default,,0,0,0,,But by that point, I'll have won.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.01,0:07:51.57,Default,,0,0,0,,And speaking of winning, watch\Nas I end this duel right now!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.65,0:07:54.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, I switch Brunhilde to attack mode.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.59,0:07:59.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, for every dragon on the field,\Nher strength increases by 300.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.35,0:08:05.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Next, I'll play this, the magic\Ncard, Enchanted Sword, Nothan.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.17,0:08:15.13,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you think of my new toy?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.57,0:08:17.81,Default,,0,0,0,,On second, sir, don't answer that yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.97,0:08:19.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait till you see what it can do.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.99,0:08:28.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, Kaiba's blue eyes\Nis gone. Yeah, but how?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.73,0:08:32.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Not only does my enchanted sword\Nremove all dragons from the game,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.87,0:08:34.69,Default,,0,0,0,,it gives my maiden a boost.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.11,0:08:39.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell me, Herr Kaiba, what's it\Nlike being a washed-up has-been?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.59,0:08:41.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Why don't you tell me?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.37,0:08:43.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Enough small talk.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.97,0:08:46.67,Default,,0,0,0,,I activate the magic card, Pegasus Wing.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.81,0:08:51.79,Default,,0,0,0,,You're no match for me,\Nwhich you never were!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.09,0:08:56.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Now all I have to do is cut my\NValkyrie's strength in half. After that,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.65,0:09:01.47,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm afforded the distinct honor of being\Nable to attack your life points directly!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.77,0:09:03.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Go ahead!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.97,0:09:05.55,Default,,0,0,0,,That card will protect me!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.17,0:09:10.27,Default,,0,0,0,,I already know the identity of\Nyour face-down card, Herr Kaiba.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.47,0:09:13.27,Default,,0,0,0,,but quite frankly it doesn't\Nchange my plan at all!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.35,0:09:14.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, Brunilda, attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.89,0:09:19.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll weaken her with this!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.05,0:09:21.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Go shrink hard!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.99,0:09:25.27,Default,,0,0,0,,And now she'll weaken you!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.79,0:09:33.91,Default,,0,0,0,,He lost half his life points!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.19,0:09:37.21,Default,,0,0,0,,This is what I like to call payback.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.23,0:09:40.55,Default,,0,0,0,,What's your problem?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.79,0:09:44.38,Default,,0,0,0,,You jealous because I run a\Nsuccessful company and you don't?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.47,0:09:45.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't you play dumb.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.73,0:09:48.71,Default,,0,0,0,,You know as well as I\Ndo what this is about.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.15,0:09:51.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Our families have been\Nrivals for generations.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.47,0:09:54.81,Default,,0,0,0,,And yours always had the upper hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.73,0:09:56.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Have you heard?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.91,0:09:59.65,Default,,0,0,0,,They're about to sign an\Ninternational contract with...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.73,0:10:00.67,Default,,0,0,0,,You're too late.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.95,0:10:02.19,Default,,0,0,0,,They've chosen us.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.81,0:10:04.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Better luck next time.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.77,0:10:06.41,Default,,0,0,0,,It was humiliating.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.25,0:10:11.79,Default,,0,0,0,,In the Schroeder family,\Nlosing is not an option.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.11,0:10:15.09,Default,,0,0,0,,So I decided to take\Nmatters into my own hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.17,0:10:16.77,Default,,0,0,0,,My goal was simple.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.99,0:10:21.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Boost Schrodercorp to number one and\Nleave the Khyber family in ruins.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.21,0:10:28.62,Default,,0,0,0,,But that proved to be a task that\Nneither I nor my father could accomplish.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.95,0:10:31.49,Default,,0,0,0,,In fact, it drove him mad.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.05,0:10:37.97,Default,,0,0,0,,With my father unable\Nto maintain the company,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.43,0:10:40.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Schrodercorp fell under new management.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.47,0:10:48.81,Default,,0,0,0,,My first act as company president\Nwas one of controversy. I
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.89,0:10:53.61,Default,,0,0,0,,decided to enter into the gaming\Nindustry a business untapped
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.69,0:10:59.37,Default,,0,0,0,,by any other company mr siegfried\Nsir i'm afraid the kaiba
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.45,0:11:02.47,Default,,0,0,0,,corporation just made an\Nannouncement they've converted their
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.55,0:11:05.79,Default,,0,0,0,,company as well kaiba corp\Nis now the largest full-scale
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.87,0:11:12.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Gaming corporation that is a lie.\NUnfortunately, it was all true. So
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.85,0:11:16.47,Default,,0,0,0,,from that moment on i devoted all\Nof my time to game development
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.55,0:11:21.37,Default,,0,0,0,,And one day it happened. I\Nsucceeded in a landmark invention.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.45,0:11:26.11,Default,,0,0,0,,that would revolutionize the\Ngame of dual monsters holographic
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.19,0:11:31.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Monster projection, however,\Nmy excitement was short-lived.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.19,0:11:36.25,Default,,0,0,0,,somehow you managed to steal\Nmy invention would take all the
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.33,0:11:38.79,Default,,0,0,0,,credit leaving me with nothing
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.87,0:11:43.69,Default,,0,0,0,,can that be true but i assure you
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.77,0:11:48.03,Default,,0,0,0,,justice will be served here\Ntoday herr kaiba your company's
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.11,0:11:52.03,Default,,0,0,0,,reputation is in jeopardy not to\Nmention the stock price of kyber
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.11,0:11:55.93,Default,,0,0,0,,corp is at an all-time low just\Nthink when i defeat you here
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.01,0:11:59.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Today, the world will see that\Nthe era of Kyber Corp is over.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.05,0:12:02.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, you really believe that?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.85,0:12:03.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.93,0:12:05.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I bet they've already turned on you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.99,0:12:10.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Now that you've finally been exposed\Nto the public as a thief and a fraud.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.37,0:12:12.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Too bad it's not true.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.61,0:12:18.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't blame me because you\Ncame from a family of failures.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.77,0:12:21.23,Default,,0,0,0,,I've never stolen anything in my life.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.47,0:12:24.67,Default,,0,0,0,,I got where I am today from\Nhard work and determination.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.75,0:12:27.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Two things you know nothing about!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.75,0:12:29.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Now let's duel!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.29,0:12:32.88,Default,,0,0,0,,And this time, when I knock you\Ndown, maybe you'll stay down!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.85,0:12:34.87,Default,,0,0,0,,My move!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.29,0:12:38.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Remember, any monsters you\Ndraw go to the graveyard!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.95,0:12:41.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, not if I activate this card!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.51,0:12:42.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Graceful Charity!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.51,0:12:48.73,Default,,0,0,0,,That allows me to draw three new\Ncards, and then get rid of two!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.31,0:12:50.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Awesome!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.22,0:12:52.21,Default,,0,0,0,,He avoided Siegfried's magic card!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.39,0:12:54.10,Default,,0,0,0,,That's showing him, rich boy!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.75,0:12:56.27,Default,,0,0,0,,What a strange twist.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.47,0:12:58.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Joey's cheering for Kaiba.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.23,0:13:00.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I discard these two.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.05,0:13:01.88,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.96,0:13:04.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Your blue eyes? But fine. Just watch.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.97,0:13:09.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Next I'll remove my blue eyes and\Nmy pitch-dark dragon from the game.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.27,0:13:11.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Which allows me to summon this.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.73,0:13:13.43,Default,,0,0,0,,My Chaos Emperor Dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.37,0:13:20.37,Default,,0,0,0,,So what?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.61,0:13:23.49,Default,,0,0,0,,My enchanted sword slays\Nevery dragon on the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.57,0:13:24.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Not this one.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.95,0:13:27.79,Default,,0,0,0,,My Chaos Dragon special\Nability sends every card
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.87,0:13:30.64,Default,,0,0,0,,on the field and in our\Nhands to the graveyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.05,0:13:33.09,Default,,0,0,0,,That's true, but there's one problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.17,0:13:36.23,Default,,0,0,0,,You need to give up 1,000\Nof your life points first.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.41,0:13:38.13,Default,,0,0,0,,And you can't afford that now.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.21,0:13:40.03,Default,,0,0,0,,There's nothing I can't afford.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.37,0:13:46.49,Default,,0,0,0,,First I play this, and next I activate\Nthe magic card, Emergency Provisions.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.87,0:13:52.27,Default,,0,0,0,,So by sending a magic or trap card to the\Ngraveyard, I regain 1,000 life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.35,0:13:53.18,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.51,0:14:02.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I give up a thousand life points to\Nactivate my Chaos Dragon special ability!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.69,0:14:22.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Once again, you're left\Nwith nothing, Siegfried.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.25,0:14:25.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Not for long.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.33,0:14:29.49,Default,,0,0,0,,I activate the magic card, Port of Greed.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.81,0:14:35.89,Default,,0,0,0,,That lets me draw two cards from my\Ndeck. Next I'll activate my magic card.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.97,0:14:41.87,Default,,0,0,0,,arms card The first thing this does\Nis raise my life points by 1,000
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.75,0:14:47.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Next we have to predict how many\Nmagic cards we think will use
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.57,0:14:51.87,Default,,0,0,0,,each turn And each of us will\Nautomatically gain 500 life points for
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.95,0:14:56.27,Default,,0,0,0,,each card But if you use fewer than\Nthe number you guess You lose 1
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.35,0:15:01.75,Default,,0,0,0,,,000 life points per card. Which means one\Nmistake and you're through, Herr Khyber.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.29,0:15:06.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I'll play Final Light!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.45,0:15:11.89,Default,,0,0,0,,And I predict that's the only magic\Ncard I'll activate during this turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.19,0:15:15.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, for the cost of a\Nmere 1,000 life points,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.25,0:15:18.02,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm able to summon a\Nmonster from my graveyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.95,0:15:21.89,Default,,0,0,0,,And I choose Valkyrie Brunhilde!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.81,0:15:27.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course, you are also permitted to\Nsummon a monster from your graveyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.45,0:15:29.11,Default,,0,0,0,,So let's have it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.53,0:15:32.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Then I choose my cave dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.99,0:15:37.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Why, thank you, Herr Keimer.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.59,0:15:41.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Your dragon gives my Valkyrie\Nan extra 300 attack points.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.47,0:15:46.53,Default,,0,0,0,,And now, my dearest Brunhilde,\Nattack his cave dragon!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.77,0:15:56.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, how many magic cards\Ndo you think you'll use?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.83,0:15:59.05,Default,,0,0,0,,You can't afford to guess wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.39,0:16:00.35,Default,,0,0,0,,I won't.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.13,0:16:04.65,Default,,0,0,0,,I predict I'll use four\Nmagic cards this turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.95,0:16:05.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Four cards?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.91,0:16:09.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't you realize you're only\Nholding one card in your hand?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.11,0:16:12.40,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right, but that's all\Nabout to change, Siegfried.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.87,0:16:16.41,Default,,0,0,0,,No, you have to be bluffing.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.87,0:16:18.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's find out.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.81,0:16:21.87,Default,,0,0,0,,First, I activate my card of demise.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.95,0:16:24.93,Default,,0,0,0,,This lets me draw till\NI'm holding five cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.01,0:16:28.01,Default,,0,0,0,,And in five turns, I\Ndiscard my entire hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.65,0:16:29.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, no!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.09,0:16:36.11,Default,,0,0,0,,And next, I play another\Nmagic card, Soul Release.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.63,0:16:40.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I can choose a card from the\Ngraveyard to remove from the game.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.27,0:16:44.89,Default,,0,0,0,,And I choose my Chaos Emperor Dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.89,0:16:50.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Then I'll play my third magic\Ncard, Spell Reproduction.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.95,0:16:56.17,Default,,0,0,0,,This lets me send two magic cards to my\Ngraveyard in order to bring back one.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.15,0:16:58.89,Default,,0,0,0,,No, you can't.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.31,0:17:00.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I just did.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.13,0:17:05.59,Default,,0,0,0,,So at a cost of 2,000 life\Npoints, I play Dimension Fusion.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.37,0:17:10.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Now each of us can bring back any of our
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.05,0:17:13.76,Default,,0,0,0,,monsters that have been\Nremoved from the game.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.33,0:17:28.93,Default,,0,0,0,,That gives me five dragons.\NHow foolish, don't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.01,0:17:31.81,Default,,0,0,0,,remember that for every\Ndragon monster on the field
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.89,0:17:36.45,Default,,0,0,0,,my valkyrie brunhilde gains\N300 extra attack points
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.53,0:17:40.61,Default,,0,0,0,,luster dragon number two\Nattack his valkyrie now
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.43,0:17:53.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, man, why'd he do that? Settle!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.71,0:17:55.67,Default,,0,0,0,,You've given up, haven't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.79,0:18:01.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, with one less dragon on the\Nfield, his Valkyries points drop.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.19,0:18:06.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Now it's time for my Chaos\NDragon to attack your Valkyries.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.37,0:18:14.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Remember,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.28,0:18:18.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Brunhilde has a special effect By\Nlowering her defense points by a thousand,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.85,0:18:22.55,Default,,0,0,0,,She becomes invincible.\NNow, Blue-Eyes White Dragon,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.89,0:18:26.15,Default,,0,0,0,,it's your turn to attack\Nher White Lightning
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.65,0:18:42.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Valkyrie's special\Npowers are all used up!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.23,0:18:46.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Which means my second Blue-Eyes\NWhite Dragon can wipe her out now!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.47,0:18:54.30,Default,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.39,0:18:56.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I'm completely defenseless!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.55,0:19:02.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm glad you came here, because now I get\Na chance to publicly humiliate you again!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.37,0:19:05.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Now take it away, Blue-Eyes!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.79,0:19:26.01,Default,,0,0,0,,This isn't over, trust me.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.19,0:19:30.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, face the facts, Siegfried,\Nyour life points hit zero,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.01,0:19:32.59,Default,,0,0,0,,that's about as over as it gets.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.67,0:19:37.97,Default,,0,0,0,,So take what little dignity you\Nhave left and get lost! Oh, yeah!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.33,0:19:39.25,Default,,0,0,0,,You tell him!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.47,0:19:40.39,Default,,0,0,0,,He's history!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.69,0:19:41.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's hope so.
